      "title": "How Tariff Refunds Strengthened Dollar General's Q2 Results",
      "summary": "Dollar General received a significant boost from tariff refunds in Q2 fiscal 2026, with refunds contributing 81 basis points to gross margin and 25 cents to EPS. The company reinvested much of the benefit into customer value through promotional activities and lower prices. Walmart and Target also benefited from tariff refunds, with both companies prioritizing price investments for customers. Dollar General's stock has outperformed its industry over the past three months and carries a Zacks Rank #2 (Buy) rating.",
